 35CL  H TYP=FUL$AUT=LIJIE SUN AND JUN CHEN$CIT=ENSDF$CUT=30-Sep-2025$          
 35CL  H TYP=FUL$AUT=JUN CHEN, JOHN CAMERON AND BALRAJ SINGH$                   
 35CL2 H CIT=NDS 112,2715 (2011)$CUT=20-Oct-2011$                               
 35CL dE EAV,LOGFT$From BetaShape v2.4 (Jun-2024) 2023Mo21.                     
 35CL dG CC$FROM BrIcc v2.3e (17-Jun-2020) 2008Ki07, "Frozen Orbitals" appr.    
 35CL dL E$Least-squares fitting is done by GLSC (version 04-Feb-2026)          
 35CL c  1980Wi13: {+35}Ar was produced via the {+35}Cl(p,n){+35}Ar reaction    
 35CL2c  with 11.0-MeV protons from the ONR-CIT tandem accelerator impinging on 
 35CL3c  LiCl and PbCl{-2} wrapped in 25-|mm Ta foil. |g rays were detected     
 35CL4c  using a 100-cm{+3} Ge(Li) detector. Measured E|g and I|g for 20 |g-ray 
 35CL5c  peaks. Deduced decay branching ratios for 9 levels, and log {Ift}.     
 35CL6c  Compared with shell-model calculations.                                
 35CL d                                                                         
 35CL c  1984Ad01: {+35}Ar was produced via the {+35}Cl(p,n){+35}Ar reaction    
 35CL2c  with 13-MeV protons from the University of Washington FN tandem        
 35CL3c  accelerator impinging on a thick KCl target. |g rays were detected     
 35CL4c  using a 28% Ge(Li) detector. Measured E|g and I|g for 8 |g-ray peaks.  
 35CL5c  Deduced decay branching ratios for 6 levels, and log {Ift}. Compared   
 35CL6c  with shell-model calculations.                                         
 35CL d                                                                         
 35CL c  1985Da04: {+35}Ar was produced via the {+35}Cl(p,n){+35}Ar reaction    
 35CL2c  with 9-MeV protons from the Van de Graaff accelerator at the University
 35CL3c  of Pittsburgh impinging on a NaCl target. |g rays were detected using a
 35CL4c  Ge(Li) detector with NaI anti-Compton shielding. Measured E|g and I|g  
 35CL5c  for 4 |g-ray peaks. Deduced 3 levels.                                  
 35CL d                                                                         
 35CL c  1979Ha04: {+35}Ar produced via the {+51}V(p,6p11n) spallation reaction 
 35CL2c  with 600-MeV protons from the CERN synchrocyclotron bombarding a       
 35CL3c  38-g/cm{+2} vanadium target in the form of VC powder. |g rays were     
 35CL4c  detected using a Ge(Li) detector. Measured E|g and I|g for the 1219|g. 
 35CL5c  Deduced the decay branching ratio for the 1219-keV level.              
 35CL d                                                                         
 35CL c  1977Az01: {+35}Ar was produced via the {+35}Cl(p,n){+35}Ar reaction    
 35CL2c  with 10-13-MeV protons from the McGill synchrocyclotron impinging on   
 35CL3c  CCl{-4} and LiCl targets and 8-MeV protons from the University of      
 35CL4c  Montreal impinging a thick LiCl pellet. Positrons were detected using  
 35CL5c  an NE102 plastic scintillator coupled to an RCA 6342A photomultiplier  
 35CL6c  tube. |g rays were detected using an 18% Ge(Li) detector. Measured E|g 
 35CL7c  and I|g for 3 |g-ray peaks. Deduced decay branching ratios for 3 levels
 35CL8c  and parent {+35}Ar T{-1/2}. Related: {+35}Cl(p,n){+35}Ar reaction      
 35CL9c  threshold measurement in 1978Az01.                                     
 35CL d                                                                         
 35CL c  1971Ge04: {+35}Ar was produced via the {+35}Cl(p,n){+35}Ar reaction    
 35CL2c  with 10-MeV protons from the Chalk River tandem accelerator impinging  
 35CL3c  on PbCl{-2} targets. |g rays were detected using two coaxial Ge(Li)    
 35CL4c  detectors. Measured E|g and I|g for 4 |g-ray peaks. Deduced 4 levels,  
 35CL5c  decay branching ratios, log {Ift}, and parent {+35}Ar T{-1/2}.         
 35CL d                                                                         
 35CL c  1971De05: {+35}Ar was produced via the {+35}Cl(p,n){+35}Ar reaction on 
 35CL2c  KCl targets. |g rays were detected using a 25 cm{+3} Ge(Li) detector.  
 35CL3c  Measured E|g and I|g. Deduced 6 levels, decay branching ratios, and log
 35CL4c  {Ift}.                                                                 
 35CL d                                                                         
 35CL c  1969Wi18,1969Fr09: {+35}Ar was produced via the {+35}Cl(p,n){+35}Ar    
 35CL2c  reaction with a proton beam from the Harwell tandem accelerator        
 35CL3c  impinging on 3.75-mg/cm{+2} KCl deposited on 0.13-mm Au backings and   
 35CL4c  160-mmHg gas CCl{-4} targets. |g rays were detected using a Ge(Li)     
 35CL5c  detector. Measured E|g and I|g for 2 |g-ray peaks. Deduced 2 levels,   
 35CL6c  decay branching ratios, (p,n) reaction threshold and |b end-point      
 35CL7c  energy, log {Ift}, and parent {+35}Ar T{-1/2}.                         
 35CL d                                                                         
 35CL c  1960Wa04: {+35}Ar was produced at Crocker Laboratory and the Lawrence  
 35CL2c  Radiation Laboratory. |b spectra were measured with a uniform-field    
 35CL3c  180|'-deflection single-focusing spectrometer. Deduced Coulomb-energy  
 35CL4c  differences between mirror ground-state transitions.                   
 35CL d                                                                         
 35CL c  1956Ki29: {+35}Ar was produced via the {+35}Cl(p,n){+35}Ar reaction    
 35CL2c  with 10-MeV protons from the BNL 60-inch cyclotron impinging on a      
 35CL3c  liquid CCl{-4} target. |b particles were detected using a conventional 
 35CL4c  thin-lens, iron-free, magnetic spectrometer. |g rays were detected     
 35CL5c  using a NaI(Tl) crystal scintillation counter. Measured E|b and total  
 35CL6c  I|b for two positron decays to {+35}Cl excited states, E|g and I|g for 
 35CL7c  two |g-ray peaks. Deduced two levels and decay branching ratios.       
 35CL d                                                                         
 35CL c  {+35}Ar |b asymmetry parameter measurements: 1993Co07, 1991Na05,       
 35CL2c  1991Mi18, 1988Ga02, 1965Ca04.                                          
